From ebb0bba3af9a4640c0a3c2e64ab6bcded788c584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:20:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-236: worgen human form - altered form drawn from
 the OBJECT_FIELD_PADDING form bit, Running Wild mount-self, two-form creator,
 human-form barber

- Unit_C: Cataclysm altered form / mount self ported from Medviten's wowdecomp fork
  (https://github.com/Medviten/wowdecomp-32-bit, used with the author's permission): GetLocalDisplayID /
  GetCurrentClientNativeDisplayID / IsInAlteredForm keyed on bit 31 of OBJECT_FIELD_PADDING (HasAlteredFormBit)
  instead of aura 302; ClientGetAlteredFormRace (worgen 12 -> human 1); IsMountSelf / MountSelf anims for Running Wild
- Player_C: a form-bit flip rebuilds the character as the other race; human emote voice in the human form
- ZepUnpackPadding: accessories are 7-bit (bit 31 is the form bit)
- DressUpModelFrame: the paperdoll / dressing room shows the human form
- Creator: a new worgen has a second (human) component; SetViewingAlteredForm swaps it to the front so every
  customization function edits it; HasAlteredForm / IsViewingAlteredForm / SetViewingAlteredForm / GetAlteredFormRace;
  CMSG_CHAR_CREATE carries the human look in a ZEPF block after ZEPO
- Barber: styles of the form showing (race 1 in the human form), rebuilt on open; CMSG_ALTER_APPEARANCE carries a
  ZEPF block (form, markings, accessories, geoset slots)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01URnr7tKsFMZq4VFsSKkj3S
